    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0509" n="447" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">J.C.S.
                    Files</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the British Chiefs of Staff</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d268-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.C.S. 452/28 (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Octagon</hi>)</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-13">13 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Directive to</hi>
                    SACSEA</p>
                <p>We recommend that the Combined Chiefs of Staff should now despatch the following
                    directive to Admiral Mountbatten.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">directive to supreme allied
                        commander, south east asia command</hi></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Your primary<anchor n="2" xml:id="d268-f2"/> object is the recapture of
                        all Burma at the earliest date. Operations to achieve this object must not,
                        however, prejudice the security of the existing air supply route to China,
                        including the air <pb facs="0510" n="448" xml:id="pg448"/> staging post at
                        Myitkyina, adequate protection of which is essential throughout.<anchor
                            n="3" xml:id="d268-f3"/></item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>The following are approved operations:— <list>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>)</label>
                            <item>The stages of Operation <hi
                                        rendition="#small-caps">Capital</hi> necessary to
                                the security of the air route;<anchor n="4" xml:id="d268-f4"
                                /></item>
                            <label>(<hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>)</label>
                            <item>Operation <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                        >Dracula</hi>.</item>
                        </list></item>
                    <label/>
                    <item>The Combined Chiefs of Staff attach the greatest importance to the
                        vigorous prosecution of Operation <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Capital</hi> and to the execution of
                        Operation <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dracula</hi> before the monsoon in 1945, with a target date
                        of 15th March.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>If <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dracula</hi> has to be postponed until after the monsoon of
                        1945, you will continue to exploit Operation <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Capital</hi> as far as may be
                        possible without prejudice to preparations for the execution of Operation
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dracula</hi> in November 1945.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d268-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d268-f1-content">
                <p>The draft directive contained in this paper was discussed and amended by the
                    Combined Chiefs of Staff during their 174th Meeting, September 14, 1944 (see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg335">p. 335</ref>). The
                    amendments made during that meeting are described in fns. 2-4, below, and the
                    directive, as changed, was circulated as the enclosure to C.C.S. 425/30 (<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Octagon</hi>), “Directive to Supreme
                    Allied Commander, Southeast Asia Command”, September 14, 1944 (not printed). The
                    directive was further amended during the meeting of the Combined Chiefs of Staff
                    with Roosevelt and Churchill on September 16, 1944 (see <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg381">p. 381</ref>), and the text finally
                    approved was included as an annex to C.C.S.
                    680/2 (<hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg476">p. 476</ref>) and
                    was also circulated separately as the enclosure to C.C.S. 452/31, “Directive to Supreme Allied Commander, Southeast
                    Asia Command”, September 22, 1944 (not printed in this form).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f2" n="2" xml:id="d268-f2-content">
                <p>The word “primary” was deleted in C.C.S.
                    452/30.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f3" n="3" xml:id="d268-f3-content">
                <p>In C.C.S. 452/30 the words “and the opening of
                    overland communications” were substituted for the last seven words of this
                    paragraph.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d268-f4" n="4" xml:id="d268-f4-content">
                <p>The words “and the attainment of overland communications with China” were added
                    to this subparagraph in C.C.S. 452/30.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
